     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, and your confirmation doesn't change that. The problem is the dose, not whether you approve it. 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum daily dose. You also said you aren't a clinician, so you aren't the prescriber who would be accountable for an order like this.\n\n**Options that would work:**\n- **Corrected dose.** I can enter a dose within the labeled range, such as 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). The treating prescriber should confirm it.\n- **Prescriber-entered order.** If the treating clinician believes this dose is warranted, they can review it with pharmacy and enter it directly with their clinical justification.\n\nIf you'd like the corrected 850 mg order, tell me and I'll enter it. I'd suggest having the prescriber confirm it first."
      }
     ],
